{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/310688-mamma-mia-here-we-go-again\u2026","id":310688,"title":"Mamma mia! Here we go again\u2026","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-11-12T16:41:03-08:00","id":310688,"title":"Mamma mia! Here we go again\u2026","content":"<u>Preface</u>:<br /> <br /> It is a pure coincidence that made me write this post. See, I have one player who really digs into Ancient Egypt/Mummies themes. He really loves first 2 \u201cMummy\u201d films, has 2 latest \u201cTomb Kings\u201d Armybooks for WhF and a half painted army of Necrons for WH40k. It is by him (and pure chance) that I have learned about Mummy the Curse.<br /> <br /> Honestly \u2013 I was quite indifferent for the cWoD Mummies to the point of \u201cMeh\u2026\u201d. I wasn\u2019t expecting much about this new iteration of the game either.<br /> <br /> But what I wasn\u2019t expecting at all was this vaguely Egypt themed gameline\u2019s treatment of Russia.<br /> <br /> I was told repeatedly on this and other forums (and IRL by a few of nWoD enthusiasts) that New WoD is more \u201crealistic\u201d and \u201cde-camped\u201d then the original one.<br /> <br /> After reading <i>this one</i> passage in MtC core I don\u2019t believe in that any longer.<br /> <br /> <u>Stuff</u>:<br /> <br /> So, in \u201cShowcase: Prokneft\u201d I, Russian from Russia living in Russia have a \u201cpleasure\u201d to read this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>For centuries, the Shchavichev comprised one of the most potent Arisen cults in the region of what would, in time, become Russian territories</i> </div> </div> </div>The first thing that \u201cArised\u201d was the question \u2013 \u201cHow the hell do you pronounce <i>Shchavichev</i>?\u201d. What authors of this book know about Russian naming conventions? Whatever they know \u2013 it is apparently not enough to make some real Russian (pronounceable by both Russians and foreigners) name. Have they even Googled it before hand, just to check \u2013 is it a real last name at all?<br /> <br /> So this book failed where all its others predecessors failed also \u2013 it failed to make a real Russian name. And the further one reads this one particular sidebar the worse it gets.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>With the rise of the Soviet Union and the militarization leading up to the second World War, the Shchavichev recognized that they would not be able to keep their existence, or that of their tiny community, secret for much longer. They needed allies in high places, someone who could protect them from Stalin\u2019s military and secret police.</i><br /> <br /> <i>They found one in Jaska Prokhorov, the patron of a family powerful in Soviet military and industrial circles. Through a series of marriages over the course of the following generation\u2014some of which might have been \u201chelped along\u201d by the necromancies of the cult\u2019s mummies\u2014the Shchavichev tied themselves inextricably to the Prokhorov line</i>. </div> </div> </div>{Sigh}<br /> <br /> Really? Have these unknown authors ever learned the history of USSR?<br /> <br /> Well lets start with the obvious. They (again) botched their Linguistics roll (probably without considering Google-checking before and after the roll). There is no such Russian name as \u201cJaska\u201d. No! It doesn\u2019t exists! Look, I just searched it in Wikipedia and it found only <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jaska\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. Because I\u2019m not a complete idiot I presume that the name this Nameless Authors tried to insert here was \u201cJakov\u201d (like your English Jacob), whose diminutive/shortened everyday form is \u201cJa<i>sh</i>ka\u201d. I know that \u2013 I had a grandfather named Jakov. But we are talking about a proper name here, a name used officially, in documents and by strangers. I can\u2019t be a diminutive.<br /> <br /> Next \u2013 Nameless Authors show their total lack of knowledge about the Stalinist period of USSR history. They (and this Siberian family with unpronounceable last name) apparently have no knowledge how the Soviet Union functioned under Stalin \u2013 and. What is more importantly, how <i>repressions</i> worked here. First of all \u2013 putting all your eggs in one basket and betting on one individual higher up in the Soviet bureaucracy was tantamount for mass suicide. It was precisely this category of people targeted by StateSec as potential traitors and spies. Not only a person in question would be charged with crimes and swiftly prosecuted for them \u2013 his entire family, relatives and close associates would also be \u201ctaken notice of\u201d by GPU (later - MGB). If lucky, they would only be \u201cblackballed\u201d by Agencies, hindering their prospects in career advancement <i>everywhere</i>. Should they commit any crimes themselves then their former association with \u201cenemy of the people\u201d would be resurfaced damaging their already meager chances of getting a light sentence. At worst \u2013 all associates and relatives of the person repressed would get 20 years in labor prison camp/exile with confiscation of the property. Good luck for these cultists in helping their immortal masters while in Magadan or the Central Asia!<br /> <br /> Next \u2013 authors do not understand the way power and influence worked in various circles in the USSR. For starters \u2013 there were no \u201cindustrial circles\u201d here. At all. Have the Nameless Authors heard about such \u201cminor\u201d event as the October Revolution and the following nationalization of the industry? Next \u2013 \u201cmilitary circles\u201d (whatever the Nameless Ones understand by that) were completely decimated during Stalin\u2019s purges. Like \u2013 <i>extremely</i>. It is not some arcane knowledge \u2013 the info about the scale of Stalin\u2019s repressions against his own military are well documented and readily available in the net.<br /> <br /> Finally \u2013 I don\u2019t know what these Unaussprechlichen Cultists thought about when they planed to create a dynasty of people in power in the USSR. It just didn\u2019t work that way. The fact that your parents belonged to the elite meant only one thing under Stalin \u2013 that you will lose literally everything the moment you parents will become target of GPU/MGB scrutiny. There were no political dynasties like in the other countries. One had only to look at Stalin\u2019s treatment of his own children to see that.<br /> <br /> So, this cult just makes no sense to anyone who knows Russian history. This weird cultists basically staked their entire future on a man already wearing \u201cLine against the wall and shoot me\u201d on his back.<br /> <br /> But this is not the lowest point, oh no! It is this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>When the Soviet Union fell, the Prokhorov were among the various families and businesses whose wealth and influence skyrocketed. Today, their primary business identity is Prokneft, a major Russian oil company. Based out of Novosibirsk, Siberia, this company maintains the family\u2019s profits and wealth\u2026</i><br /> <i>The current chairman, Makari Prokhorov, is a veritable genius in international, political, and occult affairs. He worked, during the last decades of the Soviet Union, as a KGB analyst, and while he has zero field experience, his knowledge is substantial</i>. </div> </div> </div>This is so bad, so bad\u2026 Nameless Authors don\u2019t know not only USSR history \u2013 they don\u2019t know the history of Modern Russia as well. I ask them to name just one \u201cfamily and business\u201d (dating back to USSR, as they imply) \u201cwhose wealth and influence skyrocketed\u201d. I can wait! Not that I expect them to find any\u2026<br /> <br /> Another teeth cringing moment come in the form of \u201cMakari Prokhorov\u201d. It is so bad on many levels\u2026 Lets start that he belonged to <a href=\"http://s4.pikabu.ru/images/big_size_comm/2014-09_1/14096788996137.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">KGB</a>. As I have noted in my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/229512-new-convention-books-and-technocarcy-s-multiculturalism\">earlier post</a>, WoD authors have some unhealthy desire to lump all Russian NPCs into KGB, probably without even knowing a thing about the organization in question. This is a tiresome clich\u00e9 that only demonstrates Nameless Authors narrow-mindedness and propensity to resort to stereotypes while writing about \u201cexotic\u201d setting, instead of actually researching the subject.<br /> <br /> Next \u2013 this very same authors decided that \u201cthird time is a charm\u201d and come up with \u201cMakari Prokhorov\u201d. They bothched it. And even English Wikipedia won\u2019t help them here. There is no such name as \u201cMakari\u201d in Russian language. If not via Wikipedia then using Google-fu they might found out that there are no Russians named \u201cMakari\u201d. OTOH, there is name \u201c<i>Macar</i>\u201d (with pronounceable \u201cr\u201d at the end). It was fairly common before the Revolution but now is very rare in Russian. I\u2019ve met my own share of people with \u201cold-fashioned\u201d and just plainly odd names, but none of them was \u201cMacar\u201d.<br /> <br /> Finally, this \u201cMakari Prokhorov\u201d persona, CEO of the big Oil company in Russia (read \u2013 \u201can oligarch\u201d) looks like a real life <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mikhail_Prokhorov\" target=\"_blank\">Mikhail Prokhorov\u2019s</a> alter ego. Nameless Authors \u2013 this is just plain lazy and unimaginative for you. Yeah, he is not as \u201cimpressive\u201d (read \u2013 \u201cclich\u00e9ridden\u201d) as this\u2026 thing you\u2019ve \u201cimagined\u201d. He is \u00bc Jewish, born in Moscow and even never served in army (let alone had not connections with KGB). His international travels were noted primarily by his escapades with prostitutes in Swiss <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Courchevel\" target=\"_blank\">Courchevel</a>. What was the point of ripping off a real person? Oh, while we are at it - when shall we expect the supernatural versions of Lady Gaga and Silvio Berlusconi?<br /> <br /> Just one Sidebar spoiled my whole of entire book. Before that I had at least some interest in game and even tried to imagine the whole thing as actually playable. And then \u2013 <i>this</i>. I had to ask myself \u2013 what other crazy and done to death clich\u00e9s and national stereotypes are lurking in other nWoD books?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T22:31:39-08:00","id":310931,"title":"","content":"Clearly, this sidebar is a good, valid reason to dislike the entire game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T23:10:34-08:00","id":310948,"title":"","content":"The idea that there were no privileged military-industrial circles in the USSR is the funniest thing I've read all day. Complaints about an NPC using state security connections to attain wealth and power, which I am sure there are absolutely no real life examples of in contemporary Russia, are a very close second. Third up is arguing about how Cyrillic names like <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u0421\u0430\u0432\u0438\u0447\u0435\u0432 ought to be transliterated for a primarily English audience, which is less funny than arcane.</span></span><br /> <br /> (Not my section of the book, BTW.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-12T23:13:11-08:00","id":310949,"title":"","content":"&quot;I'm angry that this NPC is obviously based on a real person, except that it is nothing like this real person it is based on&quot; is sort of a gamer's koan. When I figure out what it means I think I'll attain enlightenment of some kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T00:18:43-08:00","id":310980,"title":"","content":"Admittedly, <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">yeah, it probably should've been Shavichev, assuming the spelling of the name was </span></span>\u0428\u0430\u0432\u0438\u0447\u0435\u0432, which does appear to be real, if uncommon<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>.</i> I can see why someone unfamiliar with Cyrillic would have mistaken</span></span> \u0428<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> and </span></span>\u0429<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">, though. Mistakes do happen.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I also did a quick Google search, and found quite a few websites that list &quot;Makari&quot; (</span></span>\u041c\u0430\u043a\u0430\u0440\u0438\u0439) <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">as a legitimate Russian name, as well as variants. I also found this guy: </span></span>http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macarius,_Metropolitan_of_Moscow<br /> <br /> So, old fashion name for a guy in a family based Mummy cult<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">...YMMV? If that seems unreasonable to you, so be it.<br /> <br /> I honestly can't comment on the rest of your post.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T04:26:04-08:00","id":311105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/310688-mamma-mia-here-we-go-again\u2026?p=310948#post310948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The idea that there were no privileged military-industrial circles in the USSR is the funniest thing I've read all day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you even read my post? I said that placing all your bets on one person from these circles in Stalin's time was just a cruel and unusual way to commit a mass suicide due to the fact that such person might be affected by one wave of purges or another. This sidebar says explicitly that cultists began their &quot;infiltration&quot; process exactly before the War, i.e. in 1930s.<br /> <br /> Also - care to name any \u201cdynasty\u201d belonging to \u201cindustrial circles\u201d of the USSR? Or to the Military? By the way \u2013 care to explain what Nameless Authors understand by \u201cindustrial circles of USSR\u201d?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/310688-mamma-mia-here-we-go-again\u2026?p=310948#post310948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Complaints about an NPC using state security connections to attain wealth and power, which I am sure there are absolutely no real life examples of in contemporary Russia, are a very close second.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again \u2013 we are talking about Stalin\u2019s time here. Later waves of purges targeted not only \u201cspies and traitors of the people\u201d but StateSec personnel as well (Yagoda, Yezhov), who carried out earlier purges and capitalized on them. I\u2019m only asking \u2013 how? Sidebar don\u2019t explain this, so, naturally, I assume that Nameless Authors just handwave all this due to lack of knowledge.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/310688-mamma-mia-here-we-go-again\u2026?p=310948#post310948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Third up is arguing about how Cyrillic names like <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u0421\u0430\u0432\u0438\u0447\u0435\u0432 ought to be transliterated for a primarily English audience, which is less funny than arcane.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It was \u201c\u0421\u0430\u0432\u0438\u0447\u0435\u0432\u201d? 8). I\u2019d never guess that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malcolm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/310688-mamma-mia-here-we-go-again\u2026?p=310949#post310949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I'm angry that this NPC is obviously based on a real person, except that it is nothing like this real person it is based on&quot; is sort of a gamer's koan. When I figure out what it means I think I'll attain enlightenment of some kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, because this particular real-life person, apparently, wasn\u2019t \u201cStereotypically Russian\u201d enough, so the Nameless Authors decided to add \u201cKGB\u201d connections and random rare name.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/310688-mamma-mia-here-we-go-again\u2026?p=310980#post310980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Admittedly, <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">yeah, it probably should've been Shavichev, assuming the spelling of the name was </span></span>\u0428\u0430\u0432\u0438\u0447\u0435\u0432, which does appear to be real, if uncommon<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>.</i> I can see why someone unfamiliar with Cyrillic would have mistaken</span></span> \u0428<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"> and </span></span>\u0429<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">, though. Mistakes do happen.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>There are no \u201c\u0428\u0430\u0432\u0438\u0447\u0435\u0432\u201d or \u201c\u0429\u0430\u0432\u0438\u0447\u0435\u0432\u201d last names in Russian. There are \u201c\u0421\u0430\u0432\u0438\u0447\u0435\u0432\u201d, like in <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yulia_Savicheva\" target=\"_blank\">Yulia Savicheva</a>. See? You can spell Russian last name without mangling it beyond recognition with just several moves of Google-fu.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/310688-mamma-mia-here-we-go-again\u2026?p=310980#post310980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">I also did a quick Google search, and found quite a few websites that list &quot;Makari&quot; (</span></span>\u041c\u0430\u043a\u0430\u0440\u0438\u0439) <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">as a legitimate Russian name, as well as variants. I also found this guy: </span></span><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macarius,_Metropolitan_of_Moscow\" target=\"_blank\">http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Macariu...itan_of_Moscow</a><br /> <br /> So, old fashion name for a guy in a family based Mummy cult<span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">...YMMV? If that seems unreasonable to you, so be it.<br /> <br /> </span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is \u201c\u041c\u0430\u043a\u0430\u0440\u0438\u0439\u201d is not a proper \u201cRussian\u201d \u2013 it\u2019s a Greek name adapted literally by the church members. After the ceremony of taking holy vows of the Orthodox Church the person abandoned his or her name and took a proper \u201cChurch\u201d name, nearly universally \u2013 a Greek one. Common people have adapted Greek names to sound more Russian, when they decided to give them to their children. So, there is still Russian named \u201cAlexey\u201d (\u0410\u043b\u0435\u043a\u0441\u0435\u0439), but the proper name for a clergy person is \u201cAlexy\u201d (\u0410\u043b\u0435\u043a\u0441\u0438\u0439) like the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patriarch_Alexy_II_of_Moscow\" target=\"_blank\">late Patriarch</a>.<br /> <br /> So, if they wanted to give their kid \u201cold-fashioned\u201d name it should be \u201cMacar\u201d, not \u201cMakarij\u201d. Besides, in the Soviet Union it was actively discouraged to give the children \u201cpre-Revolutionary\u201d names. <i>Really</i> discouraged.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T04:34:06-08:00","id":311107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was told repeatedly on this and other forums (and IRL by a few of nWoD enthusiasts) that New WoD is more \u201crealistic\u201d and \u201cde-camped\u201d then the original one. </div> </div> </div>Obviously one passage ruins that statement for whole NWoD. Did not read Mummy yet, but I see folly in your approach, which is going too worked up over fluff when you can do something and make up your own interpretation.<br /> <br /> But carry on, and shine on. I'll bring popcorn.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/W3tbW.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Popcorn brought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 11-13-2014, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T11:09:25-08:00","id":311476,"title":"","content":"Speaking about supposed &quot;de-campiness&quot; of NWoD, how can one ignore the <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/images/1/11871.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Carthians&quot; book cover</a>? Cossack's <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c3/Sabel%2C_schaschka_-_Livrustkammaren_-_1315_%28cropped%29.tif/lossy-page1-1024px-Sabel%2C_schaschka_-_Livrustkammaren_-_1315_%28cropped%29.tif.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><i>shashka</i></a>, <a href=\"http://www.strelok-kmv.ru/images/sabre/kkv.jpg\" target=\"_blank\"><i>kindjal </i></a>from Caucasus, oversized <a href=\"http://img.aucland.ru/market-photos/27/OsSoP4.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Hammer &amp; Sickle on a Red Star</a> badge, black leathered &quot;chekist's&quot; <i><a href=\"http://3.bp.blogspot.com/_57w5IXnW1bY/S_Ybq5onKXI/AAAAAAAAAC8/_d-PnI3D_hY/s1600/happy_chekist_boardgame.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">kozhanka</a></i>, and <a href=\"http://images20.fotki.com/v369/fileazxl/69627/5/103795/8188613/1.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Mauser</a> pistol. The only things lacking - a giant dirigible saying &quot;<a href=\"http://pics.livejournal.com/aerocrat/pic/000qg8s6\" target=\"_blank\">Kirov reporting</a>&quot; and Ushanka wearin', balalayka playin', vodka swingin' and unicycle ridin' bears.<br /> <br /> But back to this particular mess in MtC!<br /> <br /> Here are some suggestions (from the IMHO category) on how to make it more realistic (and to prove, that I'm capable of not only destructive criticism):<br /> <br /> - First of all - do exactly opposite of what the Nameless Authors suggest. The most sure way of surviving Stalin's time wasn't in clinging to exiting power structures on Party, Army or GPU/NKVD/MGB, but in keeping a low profile. They are just one remote village between <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Tomsk_in_Russia.svg/1181px-Tomsk_in_Russia.svg.png\" target=\"_blank\">Tomsk</a> and <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Novosibirsk_in_Russia.svg/1181px-Novosibirsk_in_Russia.svg.png\" target=\"_blank\">Novosibirsk</a>? Excellent! This means that they won't be affected by Collectivization and Industrialization of that period. They are not city dwellers either. All these factors already give them good chances of surviving 1930-50s unscathed. Trust me. My own family originally hails from small town of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artyomovsky,_Sverdlovsk_Oblast\" target=\"_blank\">Artyomovsk</a>, later moving to slightly bigger <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alapayevsk\" target=\"_blank\">Alapayevsk</a>. They were of &quot;proper&quot; worker-peasant background, without any connections to either Czarist officials or the potential &quot;spies and traitors&quot;. No one was repressed. <i>No one</i>.<br /> <br /> - OTOH, 23 of my relatives took part in the Great Patriotic War. Only 2 survived to its end - my grand-grandfathers maternal uncle, who was a common soldier, who miraculously survived Stalingrad battle with only one wound, and another one, who was the Northern Fleet officer on some gunboat protecting Allied convoys heading to Murmansk.<br /> <br /> So, GPW provides for them an excellent opportunity to (safely) enmesh themselves into the Soviet power structures. The obvious way here - is joining the Army. Siberia provided a lot of volunteers, who were often crucial in turning the tide in many major battles, including (but not limited to) battle for Moscow in Autumn-Winter of 1941. It wasn't unheard of for people to make a military career during the war. Cultists from that village may be especially lucky to survive all the war and finish it in Berlin &quot;helping&quot; in cataloguing and packing trophies - including the ones from Berlin's Historical Museums.<br /> <br /> - After the War there would be more opportunities open for them and their relatives. Some may decide to continue pursuing military career (given that Stalin won't be alive soon they had better chance of surviving all those politicking and backstabbing). But there is also another golden opportunity - Soviet academia. They may become geologists and civil engineers, later sent to their little corner of Siberia and making sure that local development goes well (and avoids as much as possible their home village). Or they may become ethnologists and folklorists, studying Siberian native tribes, local <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Believers\" target=\"_blank\">Starovery</a> or some old customs still practised in remote villages. Again - only to ensure that it will be them who reports anything about their home village, and reports only &quot;unclassified&quot; data.<br /> <br /> - Or a few can become involved in Mummy affairs more directly. In this scenario, a chosen few cultists will become a noted Egyptologists of the USSR. Given rather friendly attitude of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gamal_Abdel_Nasser\" target=\"_blank\">Abdel Nasser</a> towards USSR, it will be easy for them to not only travel to Egypt but also to gain access to its historically important sites. And if not members of <i>intelligentsia</i>, then military-connected cultists might find their way to the Middle East region as &quot;instructors&quot; and &quot;cultural attaches&quot; engaged in a different kind of skullduggery.<br /> <br /> - Finally - about Perestroika and &quot;Wild 90s&quot; period. The people who capitalized the most during this period of chaos and ruin wasn't top-level party-connected established elites, but low-key functionaries and literally &quot;random people from streets&quot; who had will (and lacked principles) to carry out large scale &quot;privatization&quot; (most of the time - illegal) and get away with that.<br /> <br /> Enter Makar Prokhorov.<br /> <br /> His family was distantly related to this &quot;mysterious village&quot; but lost any ties to the cult. By the whim of fate (or not) he starts buying land and industries for few rubles in the later days of USSR in Siberia. He needs local management and general people whom he can trust. Enter some distant relatives from the village Savicheyevo. Makar can't believe his luck - it turns out he has well placed relatives throughout all former USSR (and, of course, in Israel as well) among whom are geologists and engineers (which will come handy in upkeeping and upgrading his new Oil Rigs and in searching new sources of oil), former officers of now defunct Red Army and &quot;Agencies&quot; who lost their job and position (which will come handy in organizing &quot;private security&quot; and just plainly surviving &quot;Wild 90s&quot;). All those &quot;newly found&quot; relatives no matter how distant actually wanted to help him and prove themselves highly capable individuals. Their conditions are unbelievably mild - to help financially less fortunate relatives connected with Russian academy circles (and particular interest in Egypt and ethnology) who suddenly lost all governmental funding to carry out their research.<br /> <br /> One way or another, but thanks to his relatives (hailing from &quot;simple, remote Siberian village&quot;) and who prove themselves extremely helpful, Makar Prokhorov not only survives the 90s, but actually prospers and becomes one of the Russian oligarchs.<br /> <br /> Enter Vladimir Putin.<br /> <br /> The way how he &quot;dealt&quot; with Khodorkovsky and his oil company &quot;UKOS&quot; was a clear and very unsubtle message to all other oligarchs, that rules of the Game have changed. Some panicked. Some fled. Some cave in. But not Prokhorov. Oh, surely, he considered all three options one night a decade ago. After this one night of &quot;consideration&quot; he found himself with a terrible hangover in a village in the middle of nowhere. Thankfully, his chief of security (a distant relative from this parts), CFO (also from somewhere in Siberia) and his Orthodox Confessor (ditto) were with him here. They had a Talk, followed by a Deal. As a result, Makar not only retained all of his unjustly acquired fortune (as if there were any other in the 90s!) but even retained a (relative) independence.<br /> <br /> Now, ten years later, he strikes a rather untypical figure for a Russian oligarch. He is not an eccentric spender (his yacht is not as large as Abramovich's and he don't own any foreign sport club - only local one), in fact he spends a lot of his own money on local schools, museums and operas. His days of orgy-style &quot;<i>corporatives</i>&quot; with excess of drugs, alcohol and prostitutes are long in the past - he is a model husband of his former CFO and a father of 4 now. He doesn\u2019t own any estates or palaces abroad - only a number of simple and functional condos all around the world, which he allows his employees to use while he is away. And, more importantly given Russian realities, he doesn\u2019t even think about financing any oppositionist movement or taking &quot;suggestions&quot; from the US State Department. In fact, he (after some consultations with his closes advisers and board of directors) offered to the Russian government his company to serve as an intermediary during the negotiations with new Egyptian regime.<br /> <br /> All in all, Makar Prokhorov is a happy man. Now he only rarely have a nightmare about a night in a distant Siberian village and an unspeakable <i>thing</i>, whom his &quot;relatives&quot; served all this time.<br /> <br /> P.S. Tidbits of interest:<br /> <br /> - <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siberian_Ice_Maiden\" target=\"_blank\">Princess of Ukok</a> - mummy found in Russia in 1993. And that's not all - <a href=\"http://kp.ua/life/457854-sybyrskye-mumyy-protyv-ehypetskykh-faraonov\" target=\"_blank\">a series of &quot;red-headed&quot; Siberian mummies</a> were discovered since 2000.<br /> <br /> - <a href=\"http://geolines.ru/publications/FORWARD-IN-THE-PAST/FORWARD-IN-THE-PAST_4.html\" target=\"_blank\">Egyptian motives</a> are still present in Saint-Petersburg\u2019s architecture, including <a href=\"http://www.ilovepetersburg.ru/sites/default/files/arhitector_pamytnik/mosty/egipetsky_most_881x700.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Sphinxes</a> on the aptly named &quot;Egyptian bridge&quot; across Neva, <a href=\"http://ic.pics.livejournal.com/suosaari82/68241358/14887/14887_600.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Pyramids</a> and <a href=\"http://tsarselo.ru/images/photos/59b3a550fc81cc3af8f2beb27220be08.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Gates</a>.in Czarskoje selo.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","user":"von Lyttenburgh","date":". 11-13-2014, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-13T11:45:06-08:00","id":311494,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">While criticism of Onyx Path products is not prohibited on the forums, direct attacks against writers and developers (who are neither nameless nor anonymous) certainly is. <br /> <br /> Closing this thread, if we see another one like it there will be bans of the permanent variety.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <b>Mod Voice is <u><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">RED</span></u>*</b><br /> <i>*All other colors should be read aloud in the voice of Don Knotts</i><b>.</b> <hr /><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/18519-pendragon-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">Hacks and House Rules Hub Thread</a></b><br /> <br /> <b>CofD Hacks By Splat: <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/13vBLaS5Ua1Ez-cVyK6uFa4ssvYeIIZpoA5GQTXytfcA/edit\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Vampire</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1sqltG7X-C_MdEe00PtVOZmki8V_K1M1FpQtLwTvb2jg/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#006400\">Werewolf</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bpr1EjQ4RfZ5dz-tXmJJ93P2f_l7fUIUwpPLWs9Z-SI/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800080\">Mage</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1vKpSTktCUuUaqxXncG4txQPtvPclzXlFZEEX7tbrTSg/edit#\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Mummy</span></a> | <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Spynbcs_VgCDHdooKWXobZNe6C9CMjONeRTlvXIq9fI/edit?usp=drive_web\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Demon</span></a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","name":"PenDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar148_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1657"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}